{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794801541623,"sessionID":"ses_e1d814441ffe6QmxiENmg3wjTp","part":{"partID":"prt_1e281eaba001FqML579mc4TAEH","sessionID":"ses_e1d814441ffe6QmxiENmg3wjTp","messageID":"msg_1e281dd2b001WVvrN2tEtfv5rS","type":"tool","id":"call_3669fa3c1b7646b9b9a5cfcd","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"---\ntitle: Deep Research Strategy - ux-5, offer fit, decline and refusal safety, brief wording\ndescription: Detached fan-out lineage strategy for segment five, UX lane, run against the built state after phases 016 to 033 at HEAD 84de3d600fa.\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"ux-5 research strategy\"\n  - \"command surfacing offer fit decline refusal\"\nimportance_tier: normal\ncontextType: planning\n---\n\n# Deep Research Strategy - ux-5\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n### Purpose\n\nLane strategy for the detached `ux-5` lineage. The lane covers offer fit, decline and refusal safety, and the brief's wording on the built state after phases 016 to 033 (`HEAD 84de3d600fa`). Every recommendation this lineage produces must carry a measured number or a cited file line and state what would confirm it.\n\n### Usage\n\n- **Init:** seeded below with the lane's key questions, non-goals, stop conditions and known context.\n- **Per iteration:** the executing process writes `iterations/iteration-NNN.md`, records the iteration through the append gateway, and the reducer rewrites the machine-owned sections.\n\n### Question Injection Surface\n\nExternal questions arrive through `inbox.jsonl` in this lineage folder. Direct edits to Section 3 are imported as legacy compatibility input and may be replaced on the next reduce step.\n\n---\n\n## 2. TOPIC\nSegment five, command surfacing on the built state after phases 016 to 033 (HEAD 84de3d600fa): what still limits UX, performance and cross-CLI usefulness. UX lane (ux-5): offer fit, decline and refusal safety, and the brief's wording.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\nGenerated from the reducer registry. Add external or late questions through `inbox.jsonl` in this folder; direct edits are imported as compatibility input and may be replaced on the next reduce step.\n\n- [ ] Which offer, ask and start decisions does the built brief make today, and which of them phase 020's fit guard or phase 021's head parity already settled?\n- [ ] Why did an ask offer of `/deep:review` reach the refusal decline row fresh-decline-refusal-02, and what does a declined or refused offer do on each runtime?\n- [ ] What does the brief's wording cost a model that would otherwise start a workflow: head line, directive block, command-line order and length?\n- [ ] Which offer-fit or decline-path UX gaps remain after phases 016 to 033 that no planned or built phase already covers?\n<!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n\n---\n\n## 4. NON-GOALS\n- Not re-deriving the routing accuracy floors (typed recall, false offers); the performance lane owns holdout and embedder cost, and the cross-CLI lane owns per-runtime delivery and reader gaps.\n- Not proposing an implementable patch: this lineage reports findings, measurements and gaps; implementation is a separate follow-up.\n- Not re-measuring the 033 arm's pooled statistics; this lane reads the arm's evidence and explains the UX-facing rows it produced.\n- Not re-scoring or editing the command corpus, and never printing holdout prompt text.\n\n---\n\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n- Convergence at newInfoRatio 0.05 for the configured floor of 3 iterations.\n- Fewer than 2 independent sources for a load-bearing claim: record it as a gap instead of a finding.\n- Loop budget of 8 iterations reached.\n- Any tool that would need a write outside this lineage folder is a gap, not a step.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n## 6. ANSWERED QUESTIONS\n[None yet -- populated as iterations answer questions]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n## 7. WHAT WORKED\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n## 8. WHAT FAILED\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n[Populated when an approach has been tried from multiple angles without success]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n## 10. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n[Approaches that were investigated and definitively eliminated]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n## 10A. SATURATED DIRECTIONS AND DIVERGENCE FRONTIER\n- Completed pivots: 0\n- Failed pivots: 0\n- Audited overrides: 0\n- Saturated: none yet\n- Pivot lineage: none yet\n- Remaining frontier: none recorded\n<!-- /ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n## 11A. CARRIED-FORWARD OPEN QUESTIONS\n[None yet -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n## 11. NEXT FOCUS\nMap the built state after phases 016 to 033 for this lane: what the offer/ask/start split is now, what phase 020's fit guard and phase 021's head parity changed, and which decline or refusal rows the 033 arm produced.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n## 12. KNOWN CONTEXT\n\nPrior segments (read-only, in the parent research folder):\n- `research-segment-4.md` establishes the pre-016 numbers: typed recall 24 of 44, false offers 0 of 35, brief median 306 bytes, hook median 178 ms, and the start rows that phase 016 targeted.\n- Parent `research/resource-map.md` lists the packet's source inventory; the parent `research/findings-registry.json` holds the merged findings from the earlier fan-outs.\n\nLane rulings from the lead (bind inside this lineage):\n- Phase 033's arm evidence is the entry point: pooled gained 25, lost 15, p=0.0769; an ask offer of `/deep:review` reached the refusal decline row `fresh-decline-refusal-02`; dsh started `/create:sk-skill`; devin's on-arm lost rows acted with no workflow and no offer; OpenCode delivery reads unknown in both arms; 41 capped turns.\n- Every recommendation names the file it changes, the measurable gain (with the number measured) and the check that would confirm it.\n- Never print holdout prompt text. Read-only git only. No model runs, no daemon starts, no process kills.\n\n### Bounded Context Snapshot\n\n- Source pointers: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts` (brief render), `runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` (attach/offer policy), `runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs` (offer/ask/start classification), and the phase summaries 016 to 033 in the parent packet.\n- Evidence pointers: `033-untuned-arm-arena-run/scratch/arm-evidence.txt`, `summary-arm.json`, `reruns.txt`, `arenas.txt`.\n- Integration points: the hook brief, the offer policy, and the per-runtime adapters that decide whether a model sees a command line.\n- Constraints: no writes outside this lineage; no model sessions; the arm's own numbers are the only behaviour evidence this lane may use.\n\n---\n\n## 13. RESEARCH BOUNDARIES\n- Max iterations: 8\n- Convergence threshold: 0.05\n- Per-iteration budget: 24 tool calls, 10 minutes\n- Progressive synthesis: true\n- research.md ownership: workflow-owned canonical synthesis output for this lineage\n- Lifecycle branches: `resume`, `restart` (live); `fork`, `completed-continue` (deferred, not runtime-wired)\n- Machine-owned sections: reducer controls Sections 3, 6, 7-11A, including Section 10A pivot lineage\n- Question injection surface: `inbox.jsonl` in this lineage folder\n- Question conflict owner: reducer registry\n- Canonical pause sentinel: `.deep-research-pause` in this lineage folder\n- Current generation: 1\n- Started: 2026-11-16T03:58:25Z\n","path":"specs/sys