imported as legacy compatibility input and may be replaced on the next reduce step.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. TOPIC\\nSegment five, command surfacing on the built state after phases 016 to 033 (HEAD 84de3d600fa): what still limits UX, performance and cross-CLI usefulness. UX lane (ux-5): offer fit, decline and refusal safety, and the brief's wording.\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\\n## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\\nGenerated from the reducer registry. Add external or late questions through `inbox.jsonl` in this folder; direct edits are imported as compatibility input and may be replaced on the next reduce step.\\n\\n- [ ] Which offer, ask and start decisions does the built brief make today, and which of them phase 020's fit guard or phase 021's head parity already settled?\\n- [ ] Why did an ask offer of `/deep:review` reach the refusal decline row fresh-decline-refusal-02, and what does a declined or refused offer do on each runtime?\\n- [ ] What does the brief's wording cost a model that would otherwise start a workflow: head line, directive block, command-line order and length?\\n- [ ] Which offer-fit or decline-path UX gaps remain after phases 016 to 033 that no planned or built phase already covers?\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. NON-GOALS\\n- Not re-deriving the routing accuracy floors (typed recall, false offers); the performance lane owns holdout and embedder cost, and the cross-CLI lane owns per-runtime delivery and reader gaps.\\n- Not proposing an implementable patch: this lineage reports findings, measurements and gaps; implementation is a separate follow-up.\\n- Not re-measuring the 033 arm's pooled statistics; this lane reads the arm's evidence and explains the UX-facing rows it produced.\\n- Not re-scoring or editing the command corpus, and never printing holdout prompt text.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\\n- Convergence at newInfoRatio 0.05 for the configured floor of 3 iterations.\\n- Fewer than 2 independent sources for a load-bearing claim: record it as a gap instead of a finding.\\n- Loop budget of 8 iterations reached.\\n- Any tool that would need a write outside this lineage folder is a gap, not a step.\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\\n## 6. ANSWERED QUESTIONS\\n[None yet -- populated as iterations answer questions]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-worked -->\\n## 7. WHAT WORKED\\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-worked -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-failed -->\\n## 8. WHAT FAILED\\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-failed -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\\n## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\\n[Populated when an approach has been tried from multiple angles without success]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\\n## 10. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\\n[Approaches that were investigated and definitively eliminated]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\\n## 10A. SATURATED DIRECTIONS AND DIVERGENCE FRONTIER\\n- Completed pivots: 0\\n- Failed pivots: 0\\n- Audited overrides: 0\\n- Saturated: none yet\\n- Pivot lineage: none yet\\n- Remaining frontier: none recorded\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\\n## 11A. CARRIED-FORWARD OPEN QUESTIONS\\n[None yet -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\\n## 11. NEXT FOCUS\\nMap the built state after phases 016 to 033 for this lane: what the offer/ask/start split is now, what phase 020's fit guard and phase 021's head parity changed, and which decline or refusal rows the 033 arm produced.\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\\n## 12. KNOWN CONTEXT