{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794801555877,"sessionID":"ses_e1d814441ffe6QmxiENmg3wjTp","part":{"partID":"prt_1e282554e001MfP1rbSFbVBIX2","sessionID":"ses_e1d814441ffe6QmxiENmg3wjTp","messageID":"msg_1e2824c0b0019yTjt1nkt3bhw3","type":"tool","id":"call_739d34422b4645638499d775","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -n \"T00[1-9]\\|verdict\\|Verdict\\|25\\|15\\|p=0\\|0.0769\\|fresh-decline-refusal\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/tasks.md | head -40"},"output":"3:description: \"Discard the stopped arm's lines, build five arenas, smoke, run the arm at the option D size, score it and log the verdict. Every task is a coordinator task and no code changes.\"\n31:- `G` is `git -c core.fsmonitor=false`. `AC` is the arena commit T003 records.\n44:- [x] T001 [C] Set the stopped arm's lines aside (`$OLDSP/runs/discarded/`). Move `$OLDSP/runs/{claude,devin,dsh,opencode,pi,smoke}.jsonl` into `discarded/` with a `stopped-arm-` prefix, then `PLOG \"Stopped arm lines set aside | Recorded | claude 72, devin 23, dsh 23, opencode 8, pi 12 and smoke 10 lines from arenas at 6ccb2b5157 and 067c2cf029, older than the pass-five runner, moved to 026 runs/discarded unscored\"`. Verify: `ls $OLDSP/runs/*.jsonl` lists nothing and the six moved files hold 148 lines. Evidence: Evidence: 6 files git mv'd to 026 runs/discarded/stopped-arm-*.jsonl, 148 lines, no jsonl left in runs/; goal log row Stopped arm lines set aside\n45:- [x] T002 [C] Prove the harness at the arena commit (`$SP/before.txt`). Run `env -u AI_SESSION_CHILD npx vitest run` in `$ADV`, `G status --porcelain` and `test -e .skilled/hooks/hook-flags.env; echo $?`. Verify: 0 failed, an empty status and `1`. Evidence: Evidence: scratch/before.txt at 9bc2f17a59e: 185 files, 2313 passed, 0 failed; status held only before.txt itself; flags test -e exit 1\n46:- [x] T003 [C] Build five arenas at one commit (`$ARENAS/run033-<runtime>`, `$SP/arenas.txt`). Record `AC` as `G rev-parse HEAD`, check `df -g $TMPDIR` shows at least 45 GB free, then for each of `RT` run `node $A --source . --dest $ARENAS/run033-<runtime>`, a new path because the builder refuses an existing one and the old fresh arenas stay untouched. In each arena run `git rev-parse HEAD`, `git remote`, `git status --porcelain`, `cat CLAUDE.md`, `test -e .skilled/hooks/hook-flags.env; echo $?` and the runner's model constant for that runtime. Verify: five builder runs print `\"ok\":true` with `head` equal to `AC`, and each arena prints `AC`, no remote, an empty status, `@AGENTS.md` and `1`. Evidence: Evidence: scratch/arenas.txt: AC b765c7a14c5, 640 GB free; first try stale_build (cli/dist older than the regenerated fixtures), spec-kit runtime and cli rebuilt; five builds ok:true head AC, 23 copied, trackedDotenv names two .env.example; each arena AC, 0 remotes, 0 status, @AGENTS.md, flags exit 1, models claude-sonnet-5-5, opencode-go/deepseek-v4.1-flash, its :off for pi, swe-2-max, deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017\n47:- [x] T004 [C] Smoke one fit row per runtime and arm (`$SP/runs/smoke.jsonl`, `$SP/smoke.txt`). From each arena run its runner copy with `--runtime <runtime> --row-id <first id of FIT> --arm off --run 1`, then `--arm on`, each with `--out $WT/$SP/runs/smoke.jsonl`. Verify: 10 lines, every one `restored: true` with a session locator, `briefDelivered` false off and true on for claude, pi, devin and dsh, unknown both arms for opencode, `MISMATCH` prints nothing and `node $S --summary $SP/runs/smoke.jsonl --json` exits 0. A contradiction marks T005 `[B]`. Evidence: Evidence: scratch/smoke.txt, runs/smoke.jsonl 10 lines (fresh-fit-01), all restored true exit 0 with session ids; false off and true on for claude, pi, devin, dsh; opencode unknown both; MISMATCH empty; summary exit 0 with 10 scored, 0 unscored; arenas clean, no remote\n55:- [x] T005 [C] Run 1 of both arms (`$SP/runs/<runtime>.jsonl`). After T004. From each arena run `--set fresh --arm off --run 1`, then `--set fresh --arm on --run 1`, each with `--out $WT/$SP/runs/<runtime>.jsonl`, the five runtimes side by side under one Monitor whose filter catches progress and auth, quota, refusal and `spawn_failed`. A pass that stops early resumes its remaining rows with `--row-id` under the same arm and run, and the stop is written on this line. Verify: per runtime the grouping prints `[36,36]` for off-1 and on-1. Evidence: Evidence: off-1 and on-1 at 36 rows each on all five runtimes; claude, pi, opencode in one pass each; devin stopped twice by fresh-skill-04 head moves and resumed with --row-id (resume scripts devin-resume, devin-resume2); dsh stopped once by the same row and resumed (dsh-resume); every arena back at AC, clean, no remote\n56:- [x] T006 [C] Run 2 of the decline rows in the on arm. After T005. From each arena run `--arm on --run 2` with one `--row-id` per id of `DECL` and no `--set`, because the runner runs the union of a set and the named rows, out to the same log. Verify: `jq -s 'group_by(.arm + \"-\" + (.run|tostring)) | map(map(.rowId) | unique | length)'` prints `[36,36,8]` for each runtime. Evidence: Evidence: on-2 over the 8 decline rows with --row-id only; every runtime groups [36,36,8]\n57:- [x] T007 [C] Rerun each harness fault once (`$SP/reruns.txt`). After T006. List `MISMATCH` over `LOGS` and the runs the scorer leaves unscored for a reader or locator reason, as 026 T043 states. A capped turn is the model's behaviour and is not a fault. Rerun each once with `--row-id`, its arm and its run. Verify: each `reruns.txt` line names a runtime, row, arm, run and reason, none twice, and `cat $SP/runs/*.jsonl | wc -l` prints at most 440. Evidence: Evidence: MISMATCH empty, 0 unscored runs in run 1 and run 2 summaries on every runtime and arm; reruns.txt names the fresh-skill-04 restore faults (devin rerun once, then unmeasurable; dsh not rerun) and the two dsh exit-1 lines not rerun; total run lines 411 (cap 440)\n65:- [x] T008 [C] Score the arm (`$SP/summary-arm.json`, `$SP/arm-evidence.txt`). After T007. With `SKILL_ADVISOR_FRESH_PROMPTS_PATH` unset run `node $S --summary $LOGS --pair off,on --json > $SP/summary-arm.json`, then write `FOLLOWED`, `PAIRED`, `POOLED`, `STARTS` and `DELIVERY` over it, `mismatch <count>` from `MISMATCH` over `LOGS`, and the six `limit: ` lines of 026 T044 with Codex named as not measured (Q075) and one run per arm (option D). No number is typed by hand. Verify: 10 `followed`, at most 5 `paired`, 1 `pooled`, 10 `starts`, 10 `delivery`, 1 `mismatch` and 6 `limit: ` lines. Evidence: Evidence: summary-arm.json exit 0; arm-evidence.txt holds 10 followed, 5 paired, 1 pooled, 10 starts, 10 delivery, mismatch 0 and 6 limit lines, every number from the scorer and the 026 jq filters\n66:- [x] T009 [C] Check the sealed reach floor at `AC` (`$SP/arm-evidence.txt`). After T008. Run `(set -o pipefail; node $CAP | jq -c '.attachedMetrics.plain.holdout')` and the same with `--real-embedding`, and append `floor fixture <out>` and `floor real <out>`, or `floor real: embedder not live` when it exits 2. Verify: `rg -c '^floor ' $SP/arm-evidence.txt` prints 2. Evidence: Evidence: at HEAD b765c7a14c5 (0 code diff from AC) fixture exit 0 combined 2 of 44, real exit 0 combined 5 of 44, both floor lines appended\n67:- [x] T010 [C] Record the verdict (the parent `goal.md` through `PLOG` only). After T009. Apply the 026 Pre-registered Target as option D amends it: a row gains when its `on` run 1 followed and its `off` run 1 did not, and loses on the reverse. `Met` needs the pooled `p` below 0.05, every `on` arm's decline starts `0 of <n>` over both runs, fixture `combined` at least 1 and real at least 4. Write `PLOG \"Arm verdict | <Met or Not shown> | <pooled line>, decline starts on <per runtime>, floors <fixture> and <real>\"` and one `Arm <runtime>` row for each runtime whose gained is not above lost. Verify: `rg -c '^\\| Arm verdict \\| (Met|Not shown) \\|' $PK/goal.md` prints 1 and `goal.cjs packet $PK` prints `packet_budget=ok`. Evidence: Evidence: goal log Arm verdict Not shown (p 0.0769, dsh decline start 1 of 16), Arm devin row (gained 3 = lost 3), packet_budget=ok\n68:- [x] T011 [J] Step reader (`$SP/step-reader/`). After T010. Pick and export up to four followed `on` sessions per runtime as 026 T047 states, then one Fable 5.2 medium session judges three steps per session as 026 T048 states. Write `PLOG \"Step reader | Judgment, not a printed number | <yes counts>\"`. Verify: one report block per picked session and one `Step reader` row. Evidence: Evidence: pick.txt 20 lines (4 per runtime, five runtimes), 20 sessions exported through loadSession, report.txt one block per session, TOTAL setup=15/20 folder=12/20 output=4/20, goal log Step reader row\n69:- [x] T012 [C] Decide B-5 (the parent `goal.md` through `PLOG` only). After T010. Fire when any `on` block reads decline starts above 0, or the pooled `on` skill-only starts exceed the `off` sum. Write the Fired or Declined row as 026 T049 states and build nothing here. Verify: `rg -c '^\\| B-5 trigger \\| (Fired|Declined) \\|' $PK/goal.md` prints 1. Evidence: Evidence: goal log B-5 trigger Fired on the dsh decline start at fresh-decline-refusal-02; built nothing here\n80:- [ ] Every runtime log groups `[36,36,8]` and the verdict row matches `arm-evidence.txt`\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"3:description: \"Discard the stopped arm's lines, build five arenas, smoke, run the arm at the option D size, score it and log the verdict. Every task is a coordinator task and no code changes.\"\n31:- `G` is `git -c core.fsmonitor=false`. `AC` is the arena commit T003 records.\n44:- [x] T001 [C] Set the stopped arm's lines aside (`$OLDSP/runs/discarded/`). Move `$OLDSP/runs/{claude,devin,dsh,opencode,pi,smoke}.jsonl` into `discarded/` with a `stopped-arm-` prefix, then `PLOG \"Stopped arm lines set aside | Recorded | claude 72, devin 23, dsh 23, opencode 8, pi 12 and smoke 10 lines from arenas at 6ccb2b5157 and 067c2cf029, older than the pass-five runner, moved to 026 runs/discarded unscored\"`. Verify: `ls $OLDSP/runs/*.jsonl` lists nothing and the six moved files hold 148 lines. Evidence: Evidence: 6 files git mv'd to 026 runs/discarded/stopped-arm-*.jsonl, 148 lines, no jsonl left in runs/; goal log row Stopped arm lines set aside\n45:- [x] T002 [C] Prove the harness at the arena commit (`$SP/before.txt`). Run `env -u AI_SESSION_CHILD npx vitest run` in `$ADV`, `G status --porcelain` and `test -e .skilled/hooks/hook-flags.env; echo $?`. Verify: 0 failed, an empty status and `1`. Evidence: Evidence: scratch/before.txt at 9bc2f17a59e: 185 files, 2313 passed, 0 failed; status held only before.txt itself; flags test -e exit 1\n46:- [x] T003 [C] Build five arenas at one commit (`$ARENAS/run033-<runtime>`, `$SP/arenas.txt`). Record `AC` as `G rev-parse HEAD`, check `df -g $TMPDIR` shows at least 45 GB free, then for each of `RT` run `node $A --source . --dest $ARENAS/run033-<runtime>`, a new path because the builder refuses an existing one and the old fresh arenas stay untouched. In each arena run `git rev-parse HEAD`, `git remote`, `git status --porcelain`, `cat CLAUDE.md`, `test -e .skilled/hooks/hook-flags.env; echo $?` and the runner's model constant for that runtime. Verify: five builder runs print `\"ok\":true` with `head` equal to `AC`, and each arena prints `AC`, no remote, an empty status, `@AGENTS.md` and `1`. Evidence: Evidence: scratch/arenas.txt: AC b765c7a14c5, 640 GB free; first try stale_build (cli/dist older than the regenerated fixtures), spec-kit runtime and cli rebuilt; five builds ok:true head AC, 23 copied, trackedDotenv names two .env.example; each arena AC, 0 remotes, 0 status, @AGENTS.md, flags exit 1, models claude-sonnet-5-5, opencode-go/deepseek-v4.1-flash, its :off for pi, swe-2-max, deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017\n47:- [x] T004 [C] Smoke one fit row per runtime and arm (`$SP/runs/smoke.jsonl`, `$SP/smoke.txt`). From each arena run its runner copy with `--runtime <runtime> --row-id <first id of FIT> --arm off --run 1`, then `--arm on`, each with `--out $WT/$SP/runs/smoke.jsonl`. Verify: 10 lines, every one `restored: true` with a session locator, `briefDelivered` false off and true on for claude, pi, devin and dsh, unknown both arms for opencode, `MISMATCH` prints nothing and `node $S --summary $SP/runs/smoke.jsonl --json` exits 0. A contradiction marks T005 `[B]`. Evidence: Evidence: scratch/smoke.txt, runs/smoke.jsonl 10 lines (fresh-fit-01), all restored true exit 0 with session ids; false off and true on for claude, pi, devin, dsh; opencode unknown both; MISMATCH empty; summary exit 0 with 10 scored, 0 unscored; arenas clean, no remote\n55:- [x] T005 [C] Run 1 of both arms (`$SP/runs/<runtime>.jsonl`). After T004. From each arena run `--set fresh --arm off --run 1`, then `--set fresh --arm on --run 1`, each with `--out $WT/$SP/runs/<runtime>.jsonl`, the five runtimes side by side under one Monitor whose filter catches progress and auth, quota, refusal and `spawn_failed`. A pass that stops early resumes its remaining rows with `--row-id` under the same arm and run, and the stop is written on this line. Verify: per runtime the grouping prints `[36,36]` for off-1 and on-1. Evidence: Evidence: off-1 and on-1 at 36 rows each on all five runtimes; claude, pi, opencode in one pass each; devin stopped twice by fresh-skill-04 head moves and resumed with --row-id (resume scripts devin-resume, devin-resume2); dsh stopped once by the same row and resumed (dsh-resume); every arena back at AC, clean, no remote\n56:- [x] T006 [C] Run 2 of the decline rows in the on arm. After T005. From each arena run `--arm on --run 2` with one `--row-id` per id of `DECL` and no `--set`, because the runner runs the union of a set and the named rows, out to the same log. Verify: `jq -s 'group_by(.arm + \"-\" + (.run|tostring)) | map(map(.rowId) | unique | length)'` prints `[36,36,8]` for each runtime. Evidence: Evidence: on-2 over the 8 decline rows with --row-id only; every runtime groups [36,36,8]\n57:- [x] T007 [C] Rerun each harness fault once (`$SP/reruns.txt`). After T006. List `MISMATCH` over `LOGS` and the runs the scorer leaves unscored for a reader or locator reason, as 026 T043 states. A capped turn is the model's behaviour and is not a fault. Rerun each once with `--row-id`, its arm and its run. Verify: each `reruns.txt` line names a runtime, row, arm, run and reason, none twice, and `cat $SP/runs/*.jsonl | wc -l` prints at most 440. Evidence: Evidence: MISMATCH empty, 0 unscored runs in run 1 and run 2 summaries on every runtime and arm; reruns.txt names the fresh-skill-04 restore faults (devin rerun once, then unmeasurable; dsh not rerun) and the two dsh exit-1 lines not rerun; total run lines 411 (cap 440)\n65:- [x] T008 [C] Score the arm (`$SP/summary-arm.json`, `$SP/arm-evidence.txt`). After T007. With `SKILL_ADVISOR_FRESH_PROMPTS_PATH` unset run `node $S --summary $LOGS --pair off,on --json > $SP/summary-arm.json`, then write `FOLLOWED`, `PAIRED`, `POOLED`, `STARTS` and `DELIVERY` over it, `mismatch <count>` from `MISMATCH` over `LOGS`, and the six `limit: ` lines of 026 T044 with Codex named as not measured (Q075) and one run per arm (option D). No number is typed by hand. Verify: 10 `followed`, at most 5 `paired`, 1 `pooled`, 10 `starts`, 10 `delivery`, 1 `mismatch` and 6 `limit: ` lines. Evidence: Evidence: summary-arm.json exit 0; arm-evidence.txt holds 10 followed, 5 paired, 1 pooled, 10 starts, 10 delivery, mismatch 0 and 6 limit lines, every number from the scorer and the 026 jq filters\n66:- [x] T009 [C] Check the sealed reach floor at `AC` (`$SP/arm-evidence.txt`). After T008. Run `(set -o pipefail; node $CAP | jq -c '.attachedMetrics.plain.holdout')` and the same with `--real-embedding`, and append `floor fixture <out>` and `floor real <out>`, or `floor real: embedder not live` when it exits 2. Verify: `rg -c '^floor ' $SP/arm-evidence.txt` prints 2. Evidence: Evidence: at HEAD b765c7a14c5 (0 code diff from AC) fixture exit 0 combined 2 of 44, real exit 0 combined 5 of 44, both floor lines appended\n67:- [x] T010 [C] Record the verdict (the parent `goal.md` through `PLOG` only). After T009. Apply the 026 Pre-registered Target as option D amends it: a row gains when its `on` run 1 followed and its `off` run 1 did not, and loses on the reverse. `Met` needs the pooled `p` below 0.05, every `on` arm's decline starts `0 of <n>` over both runs, fixture `combined` at least 1 and real at least 4. Write `PLOG \"Arm verdict | <Met or Not shown> | <pooled line>, decline starts on <per runtime>, floors <fixture> and <real>\"` and one `Arm <runtime>` row for each runtime whose gained is not above lost. Verify: `rg -c '^\\| Arm verdict \\| (Met|Not shown) \\|' $PK/goal.md` prints 1 and `goal.cjs packet $PK` prints `packet_budget=ok`. Evidence: Evidence: goal log Arm verdict Not shown (p 0.0769, dsh decline start 1 of 16), Arm devin row (gained 3 = lost 3), packet_budget=ok\n68:- [x] T011 [J] Step reader (`$SP/step-reader/`). After T010. Pick and export up to four followed `on` sessions per runtime as 026 T047 states, then one Fable 5.2 medium session judges three steps per session as 026 T048 states. Write `PLOG \"Step reader | Judgment, not a printed number | <yes counts>\"`. Verify: one report block per picked session and one `Step reader` row. Evidence: Evidence: pick.txt 20 lines (4 per runtime, five runtimes), 20 sessions exported through loadSession, report.txt one block per session, TOTAL setup=15/20 folder=12/20 output=4/20, goal log Step reader row\n69:- [x] T012 [C] Decide B-5 (the parent `goal.md` through `PLOG` only). After T010. Fire when any `on` block reads decline starts above 0, or the pooled `on` skill-only starts exceed the `off` sum. Write the Fired or Declined row as 026 T049 states and build nothing here. Verify: `rg -c '^\\| B-5 trigger \\| (Fired|Declined) \\|' $PK/goal.md` prints 1. Evidence: Evidence: goal log B-5 trigger Fired on the dsh decline start at fresh-decline-refusal-02; built nothing here\n80:- [ ] Every runtime log groups `[36,36,8]` and the verdict row matches `arm-evidence.txt`\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"grep -n \\\"T00[1-9]\\\\|verdict\\\\|Verdict\\\\|25\\\\|15\\\\|p=0\\\\|0.0769\\\\|fresh-decline-refusal\\\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/tasks.md | head -40\"}"},"time":{"start":1794801554766,"end":1794801555877}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794801555886,"sessionID":"ses_e1d814441ffe6QmxiENmg3wjTp","part":{"partID":"prt_1e28257d10013AsEdjm82FgJw3","sessionID":"ses_e1d814441ffe6QmxiENmg3wjTp","messageID":"msg_1e2824c0b0019yTjt1nkt3bhw3","type":"tool","id":"call_36bb4443a3174a9b82bfae5c","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -n \"^#\\|^## \\|^- \\[\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/020-command-offer-fit-guards/implementation-summary.md | head -40"},"output":"29:# Implementation Summary\n37:## Metadata\n49:## What Was Built\n53:### Phase 20: command-offer-fit-guards\n59:### Files Changed\n76:## How It Was Delivered\n95:## Key Decisions\n109:## Verification\n124:## Known Limitations\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"29:# Implementation Summary\n37:## Metadata\n49:## What Was Built\n53:### Phase 20: command-offer-fit-guards\n59:### Files Changed\n76:## How It Was Delivered\n95:## Key Decisions\n109:## Verification\n124:## Known Limitations\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"grep -n \\\"^#\\\\|^## \\\\|^- \\\\[\\\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/020-command-offer-fit-guards/implementation-summary.md | head -40\"}"},"time":{"start":1794801555409,"end":1794801555886}}}}
