{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794801659868,"sessionID":"ses_e1d814441ffe6QmxiENmg3wjTp","part":{"partID":"prt_1e283ee35001yEI9h10dDz2Ro7","sessionID":"ses_e1d814441ffe6QmxiENmg3wjTp","messageID":"msg_1e283dd5b001j1IURmVQSJyaGq","type":"tool","id":"call_12772bb88be442f0ad45426a","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"limit":45,"offset":45,"path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/021-brief-head-parity/implementation-summary.md"},"output":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/021-brief-head-parity/implementation-summary.md, lines 45-89\n45: \n46: ---\n47: \n48: <!-- ANCHOR:what-built -->\n49: ## What Was Built\n50: \n51: A model now sees the same workflow offer whichever runtime carries the prompt. On the head probe 17 of 17 prompts print the same head on Claude and OpenCode, where 14 did before.\n52: \n53: ### Phase 21: brief-head-parity\n54: \n55: The brief head is where a model learns which workflow fits the task. When Claude showed `use sk-doc → /create:manual-testing-playbook (start)` and OpenCode showed `use sk-doc` alone, the same request reached a different choice on each runtime. This phase makes the head the same everywhere. The head row keeps its command whether the request asks for every row or the top only. The OpenCode plugin asks the advisor for the same top-only route the hooks ask for, and labels its head from the first row that passes, as the renderer does. The doctor companion line now prints its policy word, `Also: /doctor:update (ask)`, and is left out when the head or its partner already prints that command.\n56: \n57: The start commit `BASE` is `7281629941`.\n58: \n59: ### Files Changed\n60: \n61: | File | Action | Purpose |\n62: |------|--------|---------|\n63: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts` | Modified | The head row keeps its command under every request shape |\n64: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts` | Modified | The companion line prints its policy word and drops a command the head or partner already prints |\n65: | `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js` | Modified | Labels the head from the first passing row and sends `compiledRouteTopOnly` |\n66: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/handlers/advisor-recommend-compiled-route-option.vitest.ts` | Modified | The head row carries its command under both request shapes |\n67: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/doctor-brief-render.vitest.ts` | Modified | The policy word, the child marker and the repeated-command cases |\n68: | `.opencode/plugins/tests/system-skill-advisor.test.cjs` | Modified | The first-passing-row label and the request option |\n69: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md` | Modified | Shows the companion line with its policy word |\n70: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md` | Modified | Shows the companion line form and when it is left out |\n71: <!-- /ANCHOR:what-built -->\n72: \n73: ---\n74: \n75: <!-- ANCHOR:how-delivered -->\n76: ## How It Was Delivered\n77: \n78: DeepSeek v4.1 flash max workers on OpenCode Go wrote one task each in four lanes that owned different files, test first. An Opus verifier checked each code task before the next in its lane, and the coordinator checked the two doc sentences directly. No check failed. The coordinator then rebuilt the advisor and ran the full suite, the child-flag run, the plugin tests, both captures and the head probe.\n79: \n80: The three prompts whose heads differed before:\n81: \n82: | Prompt | OpenCode before | OpenCode after, same as Claude |\n83: |--------|-----------------|--------------------------------|\n84: | `make a manual testing playbook for the login flow` | `use sk-doc 0.95/0.12 pass.` | `use sk-doc → /create:manual-testing-playbook (start) 0.95/0.12 pass.` |\n85: | The ambiguous review prompt led by `system-deep-loop` | `vs sk-doc → /create:readme (start) 0.93/0.12 pass.` | `vs sk-doc 0.93/0.12 pass.` |\n86: | The ambiguous playbook prompt led by `sk-doc` | `ambiguous: sk-doc 0.95/0.16 vs system-deep-loop → /deep:review (ask) 0.92/0.12 pass.` | `ambiguous: sk-doc → /create:manual-testing-playbook (start) 0.95/0.16 vs system-deep-loop 0.92/0.12 pass.` |\n87: \n88: The planned fourth mismatch and the companion lines on the probe were already gone at `BASE`, because phase 020 removed the doctor offers those prompts drew.\n89: <!-- /ANCHOR:how-delivered -->\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 90]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/021-brief-head-parity/implementation-summary.md, lines 45-89\n45: \n46: ---\n47: \n48: <!-- ANCHOR:what-built -->\n49: ## What Was Built\n50: \n51: A model now sees the same workflow offer whichever runtime carries the prompt. On the head probe 17 of 17 prompts print the same head on Claude and OpenCode, where 14 did before.\n52: \n53: ### Phase 21: brief-head-parity\n54: \n55: The brief head is where a model learns which workflow fits the task. When Claude showed `use sk-doc → /create:manual-testing-playbook (start)` and OpenCode showed `use sk-doc` alone, the same request reached a different choice on each runtime. This phase makes the head the same everywhere. The head row keeps its command whether the request asks for every row or the top only. The OpenCode plugin asks the advisor for the same top-only route the hooks ask for, and labels its head from the first row that passes, as the renderer does. The doctor companion line now prints its policy word, `Also: /doctor:update (ask)`, and is left out when the head or its partner already prints that command.\n56: \n57: The start commit `BASE` is `7281629941`.\n58: \n59: ### Files Changed\n60: \n61: | File | Action | Purpose |\n62: |------|--------|---------|\n63: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts` | Modified | The head row keeps its command under every request shape |\n64: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts` | Modified | The companion line prints its policy word and drops a command the head or partner already prints |\n65: | `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js` | Modified | Labels the head from the first passing row and sends `compiledRouteTopOnly` |\n66: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/handlers/advisor-recommend-compiled-route-option.vitest.ts` | Modified | The head row carries its command under both request shapes |\n67: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/doctor-brief-render.vitest.ts` | Modified | The policy word, the child marker and the repeated-command cases |\n68: | `.opencode/plugins/tests/system-skill-advisor.test.cjs` | Modified | The first-passing-row label and the request option |\n69: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md` | Modified | Shows the companion line with its policy word |\n70: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md` | Modified | Shows the companion line form and when it is left out |\n71: <!-- /ANCHOR:what-built -->\n72: \n73: ---\n74: \n75: <!-- ANCHOR:how-delivered -->\n76: ## How It Was Delivered\n77: \n78: DeepSeek v4.1 flash max workers on OpenCode Go wrote one task each in four lanes that owned different files, test first. An Opus verifier checked each code task before the next in its lane, and the coordinator checked the two doc sentences directly. No check failed. The coordinator then rebuilt the advisor and ran the full suite, the child-flag run, the plugin tests, both captures and the head probe.\n79: \n80: The three prompts whose heads differed before:\n81: \n82: | Prompt | OpenCode before | OpenCode after, same as Claude |\n83: |--------|-----------------|--------------------------------|\n84: | `make a manual testing playbook for the login flow` | `use sk-doc 0.95/0.12 pass.` | `use sk-doc → /create:manual-testing-playbook (start) 0.95/0.12 pass.` |\n85: | The ambiguous review prompt led by `system-deep-loop` | `vs sk-doc → /create:readme (start) 0.93/0.12 pass.` | `vs sk-doc 0.93/0.12 pass.` |\n86: | The ambiguous playbook prompt led by `sk-doc` | `ambiguous: sk-doc 0.95/0.16 vs system-deep-loop → /deep:review (ask) 0.92/0.12 pass.` | `ambiguous: sk-doc → /create:manual-testing-playbook (start) 0.95/0.16 vs system-deep-loop 0.92/0.12 pass.` |\n87: \n88: The planned fourth mismatch and the companion lines on the probe were already gone at `BASE`, because phase 020 removed the doctor offers those prompts drew.\n89: <!-- /ANCHOR:how-delivered -->\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 90]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"limit\":45,\"offset\":45,\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/021-brief-head-parity/implementation-summary.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794801659445,"end":1794801659868}}}}
