g a command names it only to refuse it.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:376:// A refusal or a question over an or-list covers every command the list joins,\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:381:// doctor command takes, so `do not run /x now or /y` refuses both.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:406:// A prompt names a command to refuse it or to ask about it as often as it names\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:493:  // that refused or asked about the command must not produce the offer.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts:1201:// refuse it or ask about it would otherwise pass that row. The skill behind the\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts:1202:// command keeps its own pass, because refusing the command is not refusing the\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts:1246:  // A command the reader refused must not pull its owner to the front, because\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:347:// particular, because \"don't add tools\" limits a change and does not refuse it.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:356:// A refusal or a question reaches its command through a use verb, so the two\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:362:// `why not` proposes the command rather than refusing it, so the word refuses\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:366:// A command the reader refuses is named without being asked for, so this list\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:368:// command so a later clause cannot refuse an earlier request, and a gap holds\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:369:// plain words only so a refusal before a comma cannot swallow the request after\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:370:// it. A reader who stops using a command names it only to refuse it.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:376:// A refusal or a question over an or-list covers every command the list joins,\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:381:// doctor command takes, so `do not run /x now or /y` refuses both.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:406:// A prompt names a command to refuse it or to ask about it as often as it names\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:493:  // that refused or asked about the command must not produce the offer.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"grep -rn \\\"refus\\\\|decline\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts | head -20\"}"},"time":{"start":1794801860535,"end":1794801861053}}}}
