-r 'to_entries[] | select(.key!=\\\"pooled\\\") | [.key, (.value.off.byPolicy.start|tostring), (.value.on.byPolicy.start|tostring)] | @tsv' specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/scratch/summary-arm.json\"}"},"time":{"start":1794801974139,"end":1794801974803}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794801974810,"sessionID":"ses_e1d814441ffe6QmxiENmg3wjTp","part":{"partID":"prt_1e288b9bc0017B9jeE8bCMREKr","sessionID":"ses_e1d814441ffe6QmxiENmg3wjTp","messageID":"msg_1e288abe200167SzJ2b964S086","type":"tool","id":"call_611e6ff2cd4e414ebedd83cc","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -n \"What Was Built\" -A 22 specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/implementation-summary.md | head -40"},"output":"58:## What Was Built\n59-\n60-`/create:skill` is `/create:sk-skill` on every runtime, with no alias. No command file is named `skill.md` now, so Claude Code lists all 44 tracked commands. A doctor prompt that says a tool is not showing up gets `/doctor:helper` beside the skills. The `AGENTS.md` Gate 2 example sends the request on stdin. Four doctor commands and `/speckit:search` carry intent phrases. A brief-cost run keeps its health records inside its own sandbox.\n61-\n62-### Phase 16: claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default\n63-\n64-The command file moved with `git mv` to `.skilled/commands/create/sk-skill.md`. Its text, its assets, the catalogs, the sk-doc hub, the `sk-create-skill` packet, the bridge entry, the hook guide, the root docs and the `markdown` agent name the new command. The deriver wrote the bridge file and the three marked blocks. The mirror sync and the six prompt and agent generators wrote every runtime copy and deleted the old ones. The old-name scan went from 55 files to 10: the nine kept history files and the new changelog entry.\n65-\n66-The mirror check holds no allowlist now. `commandVisibility` and `collapseDrift` lowercase each name before they compare it to `skill.md`, so the check fails on a command file with that name in any capitalisation. On the regenerated tree it prints `visibility claude 44/44, cursor 44/44`, from `32/44`. A live Claude Code listing of a copy of the tree names all 44 expected commands and 13 `create:` names.\n67-\n68-`STRONG_PROBLEM_CUE` reads a negated \"show up\" or \"appear\" as a strong doctor cue. Two idioms stay out: \"appear to\" and \"up-to-date\". The recaptured baseline reads `\"offered\":true` for `cmd-doctor-mcp-plain-tune-01` and `false` for `cmd-doctor-skill-advisor-plain-tune-01`. The live brief for the mcp row holds `Also: /doctor:helper`, and the CLI returns `[\"/doctor:helper\",\"run\"]` for it.\n69-\n70-`AGENTS.md` line 65 reads the stdin form. The manifest and the Cursor rule were regenerated from it, and every history hash recorded at `HEAD` is still recorded. A new manifest test pins the stdin form.\n71-\n72-The four doctor routes gained 19 phrases and `/speckit:search` gained 4. None repeats its command's tune prompt. On the real embedder, plain holdout went from 3 of 44 to 5 of 44, with typed 24 of 44 and false offers 0 of 35 in both columns.\n73-\n74-The brief-cost script runs each hook child with `TMPDIR` set to its sandbox. One run left the shared health log line-for-line identical.\n75-\n76-The `sk-doc` changelog gained `v2.10.0.0`, which records the break, and the four hub version fields read `2.10.0.0`.\n77-\n78-### Files Changed\n79-\n80-`ADV` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime`, `DS` is `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts` and `SC` is `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli`. `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff HEAD --stat -- .skilled .claude .cursor .codex .pi .dsh AGENTS.md README.md CONTRIBUTING.md` prints `64 files changed, 451 insertions(+), 330 deletions(-)`, and six new files are untracked: the five renamed runtime copies and the changelog entry.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"58:## What Was Built\n59-\n60-`/create:skill` is `/create:sk-skill` on every runtime, with no alias. No command file is named `skill.md` now, so Claude Code lists all 44 tracked commands. A doctor prompt that says a tool is not showing up gets `/doctor:helper` beside the skills. The `AGENTS.md` Gate 2 example sends the request on stdin. Four doctor commands and `/speckit:search` carry intent phrases. A brief-cost run keeps its health records inside its own sandbox.\n61-\n62-### Phase 16: claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default\n63-\n64-The command file moved with `git mv` to `.skilled/commands/create/sk-skill.md`. Its text, its assets, the catalogs, the sk-doc hub, the `sk-create-skill` packet, the bridge entry, the hook guide, the root docs and the `markdown` agent name the new command. The deriver wrote the bridge file and the three marked blocks. The mirror sync and the six prompt and agent generators wrote every runtime copy and deleted the old ones. The old-name scan went from 55 files to 10: the nine kept history files and the new changelog entry.\n65-\n66-The mirror check holds no allowlist now. `commandVisibility` and `collapseDrift` lowercase each name before they compare it to `skill.md`, so the check fails on a command file with that name in any capitalisation. On the regenerated tree it prints `visibility claude 44/44, cursor 44/44`, from `32/44`. A live Claude Code listing of a copy of the tree names all 44 expected commands and 13 `create:` names.\n67-\n68-`STRONG_PROBLEM_CUE` reads a negated \"show up\" or \"appear\" as a strong doctor cue. Two idioms stay out: \"appear to\" and \"up-to-date\". The recaptured baseline reads `\"offered\":true` for `cmd-doctor-mcp-plain-tune-01` and `false` for `cmd-doctor-skill-advisor-plain-tune-01`. The live brief for the mcp row holds `Also: /doctor:helper`, and the CLI returns `[\"/doctor:helper\",\"run\"]` for it.\n69-\n70-`AGENTS.md` line 65 reads the stdin form. The manifest and the Cursor rule were regenerated from it, and every history hash recorded at `HEAD` is still recorded. A new manifest test pins the stdin form.\n71-\n72-The four doctor routes gained 19 phrases and `/speckit:search` gained 4. None repeats its command's tune prompt. On the real embedder, plain holdout went from 3 of 44 to 5 of 44, with typed 24 of 44 and false offers 0 of 35 in both columns.\n73-\n74-The brief-cost script runs each hook child with `TMPDIR` set to its sandbox. One run left the shared health log line-for-line identical.\n75-\n76-The `sk-doc` changelog gained `v2.10.0.0`, which records the break, and the four hub version fields read `2.10.0.0`.\n77-\n78-### Files Changed\n79-\n80-`ADV` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime`, `DS` is `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts` and `SC` is `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli`. `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff HEAD --stat -- .skilled .claude .cursor .codex .pi .dsh AGENTS.md README.md CONTRIBUTING.md` prints `64 files changed, 451 insertions(+), 330 deletions(-)`, and six new files are untracked: the five renamed runtime copies and the changelog entry.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"grep -n \\\"What Was Built\\\" -A 22 specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/implementation-summary.md | head -40\"}"},"time":{"start":1794801973692,"end":1794801974810}}}}
