{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794802086784,"sessionID":"ses_e1d814441ffe6QmxiENmg3wjTp","part":{"partID":"prt_1e28a70c7001slHG7Sd0Y0hcC0","sessionID":"ses_e1d814441ffe6QmxiENmg3wjTp","messageID":"msg_1e28a1d1a001ik6ZRHdOvOx5dS","type":"tool","id":"call_2f9a77453ceb4912bd624573","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -n \"decline 8 of 24\\|decline\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/023-untuned-outcome-evidence/implementation-summary.md | head -10"},"output":"55:You can now read the packet's outcome on requests nobody tuned for. On the 44 sealed plain rows the brief carries the right command 1 time in the fixture regime and 4 times with the real embedding, against 28 of 45 and 33 of 45 on the tuned rows. On 48 new sealed rows that should carry no command the head carries one on 8 of the 24 decline rows.\n59:The capture script prints `plain_stages`, which says per split where each plain row fell out: the command led, its owner led, a route answered, a command was attached or none of these. It also counts how often a head carries a command on the 48 sealed fit rows, 24 skill-only and 24 decline, and refuses a fit row whose text repeats another row's, naming only the two ids.\n63:All of this starts at `BASE` 60968af043. The fit decline count is above zero and nothing was tuned to move it: the count is recorded as found and handed to the operator. The real holdout reach read 4 of 44 at T001 where planning read 5 (`scratch/before.txt`), the uncertainty phase 020 introduced.\n98:fit decline 8 of 24\n105:fit decline 8 of 24\n131:No task was marked `[B]`. Three follow-ups were declined, each on its task line: a rate-text assertion in T007, a refusal of one arm named twice in T018 and a shared-fixture extraction in T022.\n143:| The fit decline count of 8 of 24 is recorded and not tuned | Tuning a guard on a sealed row ends that row's use, so the count goes to the operator |\n147:| The matrix of row class by tally | Plain tune and plain holdout feed the earlier metrics and `plain_stages`. Typed and silence rows feed the earlier metrics only. Skill-only and decline rows feed `fit` only. T006 shows the earlier metrics did not move |\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"55:You can now read the packet's outcome on requests nobody tuned for. On the 44 sealed plain rows the brief carries the right command 1 time in the fixture regime and 4 times with the real embedding, against 28 of 45 and 33 of 45 on the tuned rows. On 48 new sealed rows that should carry no command the head carries one on 8 of the 24 decline rows.\n59:The capture script prints `plain_stages`, which says per split where each plain row fell out: the command led, its owner led, a route answered, a command was attached or none of these. It also counts how often a head carries a command on the 48 sealed fit rows, 24 skill-only and 24 decline, and refuses a fit row whose text repeats another row's, naming only the two ids.\n63:All of this starts at `BASE` 60968af043. The fit decline count is above zero and nothing was tuned to move it: the count is recorded as found and handed to the operator. The real holdout reach read 4 of 44 at T001 where planning read 5 (`scratch/before.txt`), the uncertainty phase 020 introduced.\n98:fit decline 8 of 24\n105:fit decline 8 of 24\n131:No task was marked `[B]`. Three follow-ups were declined, each on its task line: a rate-text assertion in T007, a refusal of one arm named twice in T018 and a shared-fixture extraction in T022.\n143:| The fit decline count of 8 of 24 is recorded and not tuned | Tuning a guard on a sealed row ends that row's use, so the count goes to the operator |\n147:| The matrix of row class by tally | Plain tune and plain holdout feed the earlier metrics and `plain_stages`. Typed and silence rows feed the earlier metrics only. Skill-only and decline rows feed `fit` only. T006 shows the earlier metrics did not move |\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"grep -n \\\"decline 8 of 24\\\\|decline\\\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/023-untuned-outcome-evidence/implementation-summary.md | head -10\"}"},"time":{"start":1794802086087,"end":1794802086784}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794802086834,"sessionID":"ses_e1d814441ffe6QmxiENmg3wjTp","part":{"partID":"prt_1e28a6e1e001pxj4S2FGw8hWxi","sessionID":"ses_e1d814441ffe6QmxiENmg3wjTp","messageID":"msg_1e28a1d1a001ik6ZRHdOvOx5dS","type":"tool","id":"call_b52f0d384f054ea9a6d2dcd4","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"ls specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/ | tail -5; echo ===; grep -rn \"Phase 024\\|phase 024\\|refusal\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/020-command-offer-fit-guards/implementation-summary.md | head -5"},"output":"goal.md\ngraph-metadata.json\nreview\nscratch\nspec.md\n===\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"goal.md\ngraph-metadata.json\nreview\nscratch\nspec.md\n===\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"ls specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/ | tail -5; echo ===; grep -rn \\\"Phase 024\\\\|phase 024\\\\|refusal\\\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/020-command-offer-fit-guards/implementation-summary.md | head -5\"}"},"time":{"start":1794802085406,"end":1794802086834}}}}
