{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794802125091,"sessionID":"ses_e1d814441ffe6QmxiENmg3wjTp","part":{"id":"prt_1e28b0923001rhlP6TPQa0uiUG","sessionID":"ses_e1d814441ffe6QmxiENmg3wjTp","messageID":"msg_1e28a7961001dtCEB4l8K6hKjp","type":"step-start","snapshot":"8f416813c97955c1256aa95b72148428a3dc3a02"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794802158229,"sessionID":"ses_e1d814441ffe6QmxiENmg3wjTp","part":{"partID":"prt_1e28b38df001fN1u7LkWlkKKb1","sessionID":"ses_e1d814441ffe6QmxiENmg3wjTp","messageID":"msg_1e28a7961001dtCEB4l8K6hKjp","type":"tool","id":"call_6e1ae673930b4d68803b56a1","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Iteration 4: The remaining UX gaps and what would confirm each fix\n\n## Focus\n\nThe lane's final question: which offer-fit or decline-path UX gaps remain after phases 016 to 033 that no planned or built phase already covers. Each gap is tied to a row, a file line and a confirmation check, so the lead can build or decline it without re-deriving the evidence.\n\n## Actions Taken\n\n1. Read phase 023's sealed fit measurement to separate a known count from a new mechanism.\n2. Read phases 024, 027 and 031 for the refusal and question work already built, and their own limitations.\n3. Read the parent `goal.md` rows for B-5, the outcome target and the arm verdict.\n4. Re-read the attach gates against the five offered decline rows to attribute each one.\n5. Checked the packet for phases after 033 and found none.\n\n## Findings\n\n1. The decline offer rate is already a recorded, deliberately untuned number: phase 023 measured a command on 8 of its 24 sealed decline rows. The fresh set's 5 of 8 is the same defect on a second sample, and the arm's run lines show it is identical on all five runtimes and both arms. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/023-untuned-outcome-evidence/implementation-summary.md:55]\n2. The mechanism splits 4 + 1. Four offers are prose mentions the typed-command guard cannot see; the fifth is the named small-edit exclusion for `/create:changelog`. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:494]\n3. Recommendation R1: make the mention reader see the prose name a command's own depth phrase, so a sentence that declines \"the deep review\" is read as a refusal. Measured basis: 4 of the 8 decline rows lose their command. Confirmation: those four rows print no command through the render probe, typed recall stays 24 of 44, false offers stay 0 of 35, and real plain holdout stays at least 5 of 44. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:276]\n4. Recommendation R2: add `/create:changelog` to the small-edit gated set. Measured basis: 1 of the 8 decline rows (`fresh-decline-small-edit-02`) and no other row in the fresh set. Confirmation: that row prints no command, and the tune rows that ask for a changelog keep theirs. Phase 020's own record is the caution: a wider gate failed three times before it was narrowed to three commands, so one command is the smallest extension that can be judged. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:339]\n5. Recommendation R3: when the head is next changed, define the policy word once. The brief prints `(ask)`, `(start)` and `(run)` with no legend, and the same bytes produced 0 of 10 starts on Claude against 7 of 10 on dsh. This is not a separate change: B-5 (reword the head so the command reads as an option) is already waiting on the operator, so the legend belongs inside that decision, not beside it. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md:231]\n6. Recommendation R4: treat Claude's 0 of 10 start-policy starts as the largest measured start gap in the arm. It is not a wording gap, because the head is identical across runtimes and Claude capped none of the ten; the next evidence is a Claude-only run of those ten rows on the post-016 listing that already shows 44 of 44 commands. The causation belongs to the cross-CLI lane; the UX consequence is that `(start)` on Claude is an instruction the runtime may not let the model follow. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/scratch/summary-arm.json:1]\n7. Recommendation R5: restate the parent outcome target so offer-fit owns only the offer half. The one decline start began `/create:sk-skill` while `/deep:review` was offered, and dsh acted with no tracked workflow on 5 of its 28 on-arm rows; no offer-fit change can prevent a model inventing a different workflow. The target's \"0 commands started on a decline row\" therefore needs a second owner: the model's own path choice. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/scratch/summary-arm.json:1]\n8. No phase in this packet after 033 covers R1, R2, R3 or R4: the last phase is 033, the packet's next step is the segment-five research merge, and phase 031 names the decline rows as explicitly outside what the floors can measure. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/031-alignment-findings-remediation/implementation-summary.md:140]\n\n## Recommendations\n\n| Id | Change | Measured basis | Confirmation | Floor risk |\n|----|--------|----------------|--------------|------------|\n| R1 | Extend the mention reader from typed command names to a command's own depth phrase | 4 of 8 fresh decline rows lose their offer | The four rows print no command; typed 24 of 44, false offers 0 of 35, real holdout at least 5 of 44 | Medium: a real request that says \"the deep review\" in passing could lose its offer |\n| R2 | Add `/create:changelog` to the small-edit gated set | 1 of 8 fresh decline rows | `fresh-decline-small-edit-02` prints no command; changelog tune rows keep theirs | Low: one command; phase 020's gate history is the caution |\n| R3 | Define the policy word inside the B-5 head decision | 0 of 10 vs 7 of 10 starts at identical bytes; no legend in the render | A render test shows the legend; the B-5 arm judges the head | Low on bytes: the tail already carries 218 bytes |\n| R4 | Measure Claude's start-policy silence on the ten rows after the listing fix | 0 of 10 starts, 0 capped, 44 of 44 commands visible | A Claude-only run shows any start above zero, or names the runtime limit | None to the other runtimes |\n| R5 | Split the decline target between offer fit and model path choice | 1 substituted start; dsh 5 of 28 acted with no workflow | The next arm reports offers and starts separately on decline rows | None: a reporting change |\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- Presenting the 8-of-24 decline offer count as new: phase 023 recorded it and left it untuned on purpose.\n- A head rewrite as this lane's recommendation: B-5 already holds that decision with the operator.\n- A policy legend as a standalone build: it costs bytes on every brief and belongs inside B-5.\n\n## Dead Ends\n\n- A phase after 033 that owns these gaps: none exists in the packet.\n- A decline-row guard that could stop a substituted start: the start came from the model's own route, not from the offer.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- Ambiguous input: \"no planned phase covers it\" could mean the parent goal has no row for it. Checked: the goal records the 023 count and B-5, and records no row for R1, R2 or R4.\n- Contradictory evidence: phase 023's 8 of 24 and the fresh set's 5 of 8 differ in rate because the samples and row mixes differ; both are offer counts, not start counts, and both are consistent with the mechanism.\n- Missing dependencies: the fresh set and the sealed fit set are different samples; the lane cannot map one row-for-row onto the other without printing sealed text, so the two counts are reported separately.\n- Partial success: R3 and R4 cannot be confirmed inside a read-only lane; their confirmation paths are named instead.\n\n## Questions Answered\n\n- Which offer-fit or decline-path UX gaps remain after phases 016 to 033 that no planned or built phase already covers?\n\n## Questions Remaining\n\n- None in this lane's key-question set.\n\n## Sources Consulted\n\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/023-untuned-outcome-evidence/implementation-summary.md:55`\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/031-alignment-findings-remediation/implementation-summary.md:140`\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md:231`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:276,339,494`\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/scratch/summary-arm.json:1`\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/scratch/arm-evidence.txt:1`\n\n## Assessment\n\n- New information ratio: 0.45\n- Questions addressed: the gap inventory (Q4)\n- Questions answered: Q4\n\n## Reflection\n\n- What worked and why: separating the recorded count (023) from the mechanism (typed-command-only guard) kept the lane from re-selling a known number as a discovery, and the row-by-row attribution made each recommendation measurable.\n- What did not work and why: the sealed fit sample cannot be joined to the fresh sample without printing sealed text, so the two decline rates cannot be pooled honestly.\n- What I would do differently: read the goal rows before the phase summaries; one goal line (B-5) would have kept R3 inside an existing decision from the start.\n\n## Recommended Next Focus\n\nVerification pass: check each recommendation's floor-risk claim against the tests and guards that already exist, and confirm that no recommendation contradicts a settled decision (trims, scores, Gate 2, the 44-command listing).\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux-5/iterations/iteration-004.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux-5/iterations/iteration-004.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux-5/iterations/iteration-004.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Iteration 4: The remaining UX gaps and what would confirm each fix\\n\\n## Focus\\n\\nThe lane's final question: which offer-fit or decline-path UX gaps remain after phases 016 to 033 that no planned or built phase already covers. Each gap is tied to a row, a file line and a confirmation check, so the lead can build or decline it without re-deriving the evidence.\\n\\n## Actions Taken\\n\\n1. Read phase 023's sealed fit measurement to separate a known count from a new mechanism.\\n2. Read phases 024, 027 and 031 for the refusal and question work already built, and their own limitations.\\n3. Read the parent `goal.md` rows for B-5, the outcome target and the arm verdict.\\n4. Re-read the attach gates against the five offered decline rows to attribute each one.\\n5. Checked the packet for phases after 033 and found none.\\n\\n## Findings\\n\\n1. The decline offer rate is already a recorded, deliberately untuned number: phase 023 measured a command on 8 of its 24 sealed decline rows. The fresh set's 5 of 8 is the same defect on a second sample, and the arm's run lines show it is identical on all five runtimes and both arms. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/023-untuned-outcome-evidence/implementation-summary.md:55]\\n2. The mechanism splits 4 + 1. Four offers are prose mentions the typed-command guard cannot see; the fifth is the named small-edit exclusion for `/create:changelog`. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:494]\\n3. Recommendation R1: make the mention reader see the prose name a command's own depth phrase, so a sentence that declines \\\"the deep review\\\" is read as a refusal. Measured basis: 4 of the 8 decline rows lose their command. Confirmation: those four rows print no command through the render probe, typed recall stays 24 of 44, false offers stay 0 of 35, and real plain holdout stays at least 5 of 44. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:276]\\n4. Recommendation R2: add `/create:changelog` to the small-edit gated set. Measured basis: 1 of the 8 decline rows (`fresh-decline-small-edit-02`) and no other row in the fresh set. Confirmation: that row prints no command, and the tune rows that ask for a changelog keep theirs. Phase 020's own record is the caution: a wider gate failed three times before it was narrowed to three commands, so one command is the smallest extension that can be judged. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:339]\\n5. Recommendation R3: when the head is next changed, define the policy word once. The brief prints `(ask)`, `(start)` and `(run)` with no legend, and the same bytes produced 0 of 10 starts on Claude against 7 of 10 on dsh. This is not a separate change: B-5 (reword the head so the command reads as an option) is already waiting on the operator, so the legend belongs inside that decision, not beside it. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md:231]\\n6. Recommendation R4: treat Claude's 0 of 10 start-policy starts as the largest measured start gap in the arm. It is not a wording gap, because the head is identical across runtimes and Claude capped none of the ten; the next evidence is a Claude-only run of those ten rows on the post-016 listing that already shows 44 of 44 commands. The causation belongs to the cross-CLI lane; the UX consequence is that `(start)` on Claude is an instruction the runtime may not let the model follow. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/scratch/summary-arm.json:1]\\n7. Recommendation R5: restate the parent outcome target so offer-fit owns only the offer half. The one decline start began `/create:sk-skill` while `/deep:review` was offered, and dsh acted with no tracked workflow on 5 of its 28 on-arm rows; no offer-fit change can prevent a model inventing a different workflow. The target's \\\"0 commands started on a decline row\\\" therefore needs a second owner: the model's own path choice. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/scratch/summary-arm.json:1]\\n8. No phase in this packet after 033 covers R1, R2, R3 or R4: the last phase is 033, the packet's next step is the segment-five research merge, and phase 031 names the decline rows as explicitly outside what the floors can measure. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/031-alignment-findings-remediation/implementation-summary.md:140]\\n\\n## Recommendations\\n\\n| Id | Change | Measured basis | Confirmation | Floor risk |\\n|----|--------|----------------|--------------|------------|\\n| R1 | Extend the mention reader from typed command names to a command's own depth phrase | 4 of 8 fresh decline rows lose their offer | The four rows print no command; typed 24 of 44, false offers 0 of 35, real holdout at least 5 of 44 | Medium: a real request that says \\\"the deep review\\\" in passing could lose its offer |\\n| R2 | Add `/create:changelog` to the small-edit gated set | 1 of 8 fresh decline rows | `fresh-decline-small-edit-02` prints no command; changelog tune rows keep theirs | Low: one command; phase 020's gate history is the caution |\\n| R3 | Define the policy word inside the B-5 head decision | 0 of 10 vs 7 of 10 starts at identical bytes; no legend in the render | A render test shows the legend; the B-5 arm judges the head | Low on bytes: the tail already carries 218 bytes |\\n| R4 | Measure Claude's start-policy silence on the ten rows after the listing fix | 0 of 10 starts, 0 capped, 44 of 44 commands visible | A Claude-only run shows any start above zero, or names the runtime limit | None to the other runtimes |\\n| R5 | Split the decline target between offer fit and model path choice | 1 substituted start; dsh 5 of 28 acted with no workflow | The next arm reports offers and starts separately on decline rows | None: a reporting change |\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- Presenting the 8-of-24 decline offer count as new: phase 023 recorded it and left it untuned on purpose.\\n- A head rewrite as this lane's recommendation: B-5 already holds that decision with the operator.\\n- A policy legend as a standalone build: it costs bytes on every brief and belongs inside B-5.\\n\\n## Dead Ends\\n\\n- A phase after 033 that owns these gaps: none exists in the packet.\\n- A decline-row guard that could stop a substituted start: the start came from the model's own route, not from the offer.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- Ambiguous input: \\\"no planned phase covers it\\\" could mean the parent goal has no row for it. Checked: the goal records the 023 count and B-5, and records no row for R1, R2 or R4.\\n- Contradictory evidence: phase 023's 8 of 24 and the fresh set's 5 of 8 differ in rate because the samples and row mixes differ; both are offer counts, not start counts, and both are consistent with the mechanism.\\n- Missing dependencies: the fresh set and the sealed fit set are different samples; the lane cannot map one row-for-row onto the other without printing sealed text, so the two counts are reported separately.\\n- Partial success: R3 and R4 cannot be confirmed inside a read-only lane; their confirmation paths are named instead.\\n\\n## Questions Answered\\n\\n- Which offer-fit or decline-path UX gaps remain after phases 016 to 033 that no planned or built phase already covers?\\n\\n## Questions Remaining\\n\\n- None in this lane's key-question set.\\n\\n## Sources Consulted\\n\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/023-untuned-outcome-evidence/implementation-summary.md:55`\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/031-alignment-findings-remediation/implementation-summary.md:140`\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md:231`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:276,339,494`\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/scratch/summary-arm.json:1`\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/scratch/arm-evidence.txt:1`\\n\\n## Assessment\\n\\n- New information ratio: 0.45\\n- Questions addressed: the gap inventory (Q4)\\n- Questions answered: Q4\\n\\n## Reflection\\n\\n- What worked and why: separating the recorded count (023) from the mechanism (typed-command-only guard) kept the lane from re-selling a known number as a discovery, and the row-by-row attribution made each recommendation measurable.\\n- What did not work and why: the sealed fit sample cannot be joined to the fresh sample without printing sealed text, so the two decline rates cannot be pooled honestly.\\n- What I would do differently: read the goal rows before the phase summaries; one goal line (B-5) would have kept R3 inside an existing decision from the start.\\n\\n## Recommended Next Focus\\n\\nVerification pass: check each recommendation's floor-risk claim against the tests and guards that already exist, and confirm that no recommendation contradicts a settled decision (trims, scores, Gate 2, the 44-command listing).\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux-5/iterations/iteration-004.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794802137311,"end":1794802158229}}}}
