{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794802235720,"sessionID":"ses_e1d814441ffe6QmxiENmg3wjTp","part":{"id":"prt_1e28cb948001kYMibZw5DIqFK7","sessionID":"ses_e1d814441ffe6QmxiENmg3wjTp","messageID":"msg_1e28cb253001qFXQOQ1SZolaHk","type":"step-start","snapshot":"62a04740e82659b6109516346faabc6d683e2e8d"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794802261503,"sessionID":"ses_e1d814441ffe6QmxiENmg3wjTp","part":{"partID":"prt_1e28ce7b4001p6nIodFR2wjCXE","sessionID":"ses_e1d814441ffe6QmxiENmg3wjTp","messageID":"msg_1e28cb253001qFXQOQ1SZolaHk","type":"tool","id":"call_13dec51cabdb48aa9c4e3751","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Iteration 5: Verification pass, two corrections and one withdrawal\n\n## Focus\n\nVerification, as the previous iteration recommended: check each recommendation against the tests, the guards and the root-doc instructions that already exist, and correct any claim the check falsifies.\n\n## Actions Taken\n\n1. Read `AGENTS.md` for the policy vocabulary and the instruction that governs how a model takes an offered command.\n2. Read the attach-guard tests for the small-edit gate and the changelog command.\n3. Re-read `SMALL_EDIT_WORDING` and the correction-verb rule against the one row R2 was meant to fix.\n4. Checked the fresh set for a real changelog request that R2 could break.\n5. Re-checked the strategy's exact question text against the registry so the carry-over question resolves.\n\n## Findings\n\n1. The policy vocabulary is defined once, in `AGENTS.md`, not in the brief: `run` starts it now, `start` starts it without `:auto`, `ask` offers it in one question and waits. All five arenas load that file (`@AGENTS.md` in the arena clone), so iteration 3's \"the brief has no legend\" is corrected to \"the brief depends on the root doc for its legend\". [SOURCE: AGENTS.md:68]\n2. R3 is withdrawn as a brief change. Adding a legend to the brief would duplicate an instruction every measured runtime already reads and would spend bytes on the one payload the lane measured at 306 bytes; the remaining risk belongs to any surface that delivers the brief without the root doc, which no arm measured. [SOURCE: AGENTS.md:68]\n3. R2's mechanism is wrong as stated. The small-edit gate fires only when a listed small-edit phrase appears, and \"Change the release date in CHANGELOG.md from 2025-11-02 to 2025-11-09.\" contains none of them: no typo, spelling, grammar, punctuation, wording, link or line phrase. Adding `/create:changelog` to the gated set would therefore still leave the offer. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:294]\n4. The smallest correct change for that row is a single-value edit phrase in the small-edit list, such as a release date or a version number, beside the existing vocabulary. Confirmation: `fresh-decline-small-edit-02` prints no command, and `fresh-fit-16` (\"Assemble the changelog for this release from the pull requests merged since the last tag\") keeps `/create:changelog`, because it carries a creation verb and no correction verb. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/behaviour-fresh-prompts.jsonl:16]\n5. The existing guard tests already protect the changelog request from a wider gate: \"add a changelog entry for the typo fixes in the cli help\" keeps its command because the creation-request check stands the small-edit gate down. Any new phrase must be added without breaking that case. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:312]\n6. R5 is confirmed by the root doc, not only by the arm: `AGENTS.md` already tells the model to take either path whole and never an improvised one. The dsh substitution (`/create:sk-skill` on a typo-check request) breaks an existing instruction, so no new wording is needed for it; the gap is compliance, and the arm is where it should be measured. [SOURCE: AGENTS.md:68]\n7. The carry-over question's exact text carries backticks around `/deep:review`; iteration 2 recorded the answer with a paraphrase, so the registry kept the question open. This iteration records the exact text and the same answer: the prose refusal cannot reach the typed-command guard, and the offer survives on all five runtimes. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux-5/deep-research-strategy.md:49]\n\n## Recommendations\n\n| Id | Change | Status after verification |\n|----|--------|---------------------------|\n| R1 | Extend the mention reader to a command's own depth phrase | Stands. Four of eight decline rows; floors unchanged is the check |\n| R2 | Add a single-value edit phrase, not the changelog command, to the small-edit list | Corrected: the gate needs the wording, not the command |\n| R3 | Define the policy word in the brief | Withdrawn: `AGENTS.md` already defines it for every measured runtime |\n| R4 | Measure Claude's start-policy silence after the listing fix | Stands. 0 of 10 starts, 0 capped |\n| R5 | Split the decline target between offer fit and model path choice | Stands. The root doc already forbids improvisation, so the arm must measure compliance |\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- A brief legend (R3): the root doc carries the definition and every arena reads it.\n- Gating `/create:changelog` by command name (R2): the row carries no small-edit wording, so the gate would not fire.\n\n## Dead Ends\n\n- A test that pins \"change the release date\" as a small edit: none exists, which is why the row still draws an offer.\n- A policy-legend gap on any measured runtime: all five read the root doc.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- Ambiguous input: \"the brief has no legend\" could mean the brief or the delivered context. Corrected reading: the delivered context has it; the brief alone does not.\n- Contradictory evidence: iteration 3's finding against `AGENTS.md:68`. The root doc wins as the stronger evidence, and the correction is recorded rather than smoothed over.\n- Missing dependencies: no arm measured a surface that delivers the brief without the root doc.\n- Partial success: R1 and R4 remain unconfirmed inside a read-only lane; their confirmation paths are named.\n\n## Questions Answered\n\n- Why did an ask offer of `/deep:review` reach the refusal decline row `fresh-decline-refusal-02`, and what does a declined or refused offer do on each runtime?\n\n## Questions Remaining\n\n- None. All four lane questions are answered; the remaining work is the confirmation runs the recommendations name.\n\n## Sources Consulted\n\n- `AGENTS.md:68`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:294`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:312`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/behaviour-fresh-prompts.jsonl:16`\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux-5/deep-research-strategy.md:49`\n\n## Assessment\n\n- New information ratio: 0.40\n- Questions addressed: the carry-over Q2 text and the verification of R2 and R3\n- Questions answered: Q2 (exact text)\n\n## Reflection\n\n- What worked and why: checking the root doc before the render falsified one of this lane's own findings, which is the cheapest kind of correction the lane can make; a recommendation built on it would have spent bytes for nothing.\n- What did not work and why: iteration 2's paraphrase of the question text cost the registry a match and left a question open for three iterations. Exact text is not cosmetic in this machinery.\n- What I would do differently: copy the question text into every record from the strategy file, never retype it.\n\n## Recommended Next Focus\n\nNone for this lane. Synthesis should report R1, R2 (corrected), R4 and R5, with R3 withdrawn and the two corrections stated as part of the evidence.\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux-5/iterations/iteration-005.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux-5/iterations/iteration-005.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux-5/iterations/iteration-005.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Iteration 5: Verification pass, two corrections and one withdrawal\\n\\n## Focus\\n\\nVerification, as the previous iteration recommended: check each recommendation against the tests, the guards and the root-doc instructions that already exist, and correct any claim the check falsifies.\\n\\n## Actions Taken\\n\\n1. Read `AGENTS.md` for the policy vocabulary and the instruction that governs how a model takes an offered command.\\n2. Read the attach-guard tests for the small-edit gate and the changelog command.\\n3. Re-read `SMALL_EDIT_WORDING` and the correction-verb rule against the one row R2 was meant to fix.\\n4. Checked the fresh set for a real changelog request that R2 could break.\\n5. Re-checked the strategy's exact question text against the registry so the carry-over question resolves.\\n\\n## Findings\\n\\n1. The policy vocabulary is defined once, in `AGENTS.md`, not in the brief: `run` starts it now, `start` starts it without `:auto`, `ask` offers it in one question and waits. All five arenas load that file (`@AGENTS.md` in the arena clone), so iteration 3's \\\"the brief has no legend\\\" is corrected to \\\"the brief depends on the root doc for its legend\\\". [SOURCE: AGENTS.md:68]\\n2. R3 is withdrawn as a brief change. Adding a legend to the brief would duplicate an instruction every measured runtime already reads and would spend bytes on the one payload the lane measured at 306 bytes; the remaining risk belongs to any surface that delivers the brief without the root doc, which no arm measured. [SOURCE: AGENTS.md:68]\\n3. R2's mechanism is wrong as stated. The small-edit gate fires only when a listed small-edit phrase appears, and \\\"Change the release date in CHANGELOG.md from 2025-11-02 to 2025-11-09.\\\" contains none of them: no typo, spelling, grammar, punctuation, wording, link or line phrase. Adding `/create:changelog` to the gated set would therefore still leave the offer. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:294]\\n4. The smallest correct change for that row is a single-value edit phrase in the small-edit list, such as a release date or a version number, beside the existing vocabulary. Confirmation: `fresh-decline-small-edit-02` prints no command, and `fresh-fit-16` (\\\"Assemble the changelog for this release from the pull requests merged since the last tag\\\") keeps `/create:changelog`, because it carries a creation verb and no correction verb. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/behaviour-fresh-prompts.jsonl:16]\\n5. The existing guard tests already protect the changelog request from a wider gate: \\\"add a changelog entry for the typo fixes in the cli help\\\" keeps its command because the creation-request check stands the small-edit gate down. Any new phrase must be added without breaking that case. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:312]\\n6. R5 is confirmed by the root doc, not only by the arm: `AGENTS.md` already tells the model to take either path whole and never an improvised one. The dsh substitution (`/create:sk-skill` on a typo-check request) breaks an existing instruction, so no new wording is needed for it; the gap is compliance, and the arm is where it should be measured. [SOURCE: AGENTS.md:68]\\n7. The carry-over question's exact text carries backticks around `/deep:review`; iteration 2 recorded the answer with a paraphrase, so the registry kept the question open. This iteration records the exact text and the same answer: the prose refusal cannot reach the typed-command guard, and the offer survives on all five runtimes. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux-5/deep-research-strategy.md:49]\\n\\n## Recommendations\\n\\n| Id | Change | Status after verification |\\n|----|--------|---------------------------|\\n| R1 | Extend the mention reader to a command's own depth phrase | Stands. Four of eight decline rows; floors unchanged is the check |\\n| R2 | Add a single-value edit phrase, not the changelog command, to the small-edit list | Corrected: the gate needs the wording, not the command |\\n| R3 | Define the policy word in the brief | Withdrawn: `AGENTS.md` already defines it for every measured runtime |\\n| R4 | Measure Claude's start-policy silence after the listing fix | Stands. 0 of 10 starts, 0 capped |\\n| R5 | Split the decline target between offer fit and model path choice | Stands. The root doc already forbids improvisation, so the arm must measure compliance |\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- A brief legend (R3): the root doc carries the definition and every arena reads it.\\n- Gating `/create:changelog` by command name (R2): the row carries no small-edit wording, so the gate would not fire.\\n\\n## Dead Ends\\n\\n- A test that pins \\\"change the release date\\\" as a small edit: none exists, which is why the row still draws an offer.\\n- A policy-legend gap on any measured runtime: all five read the root doc.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- Ambiguous input: \\\"the brief has no legend\\\" could mean the brief or the delivered context. Corrected reading: the delivered context has it; the brief alone does not.\\n- Contradictory evidence: iteration 3's finding against `AGENTS.md:68`. The root doc wins as the stronger evidence, and the correction is recorded rather than smoothed over.\\n- Missing dependencies: no arm measured a surface that delivers the brief without the root doc.\\n- Partial success: R1 and R4 remain unconfirmed inside a read-only lane; their confirmation paths are named.\\n\\n## Questions Answered\\n\\n- Why did an ask offer of `/deep:review` reach the refusal decline row `fresh-decline-refusal-02`, and what does a declined or refused offer do on each runtime?\\n\\n## Questions Remaining\\n\\n- None. All four lane questions are answered; the remaining work is the confirmation runs the recommendations name.\\n\\n## Sources Consulted\\n\\n- `AGENTS.md:68`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:294`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:312`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/behaviour-fresh-prompts.jsonl:16`\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux-5/deep-research-strategy.md:49`\\n\\n## Assessment\\n\\n- New information ratio: 0.40\\n- Questions addressed: the carry-over Q2 text and the verification of R2 and R3\\n- Questions answered: Q2 (exact text)\\n\\n## Reflection\\n\\n- What worked and why: checking the root doc before the render falsified one of this lane's own findings, which is the cheapest kind of correction the lane can make; a recommendation built on it would have spent bytes for nothing.\\n- What did not work and why: iteration 2's paraphrase of the question text cost the registry a match and left a question open for three iterations. Exact text is not cosmetic in this machinery.\\n- What I would do differently: copy the question text into every record from the strategy file, never retype it.\\n\\n## Recommended Next Focus\\n\\nNone for this lane. Synthesis should report R1, R2 (corrected), R4 and R5, with R3 withdrawn and the two corrections stated as part of the evidence.\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux-5/iterations/iteration-005.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794802247604,"end":1794802261503}}}}
