{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794802586546,"sessionID":"ses_e1d814441ffe6QmxiENmg3wjTp","part":{"id":"prt_1e29213b2001ja45FiBEnyjCIN","sessionID":"ses_e1d814441ffe6QmxiENmg3wjTp","messageID":"msg_1e2920b74001Ivn2LxOAgILdTJ","type":"step-start","snapshot":"2d1f53770ca1196a9010afa14d9477048d98a88e"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794802603168,"sessionID":"ses_e1d814441ffe6QmxiENmg3wjTp","part":{"partID":"prt_1e2921e52002OKa0d0nXZau0zO","sessionID":"ses_e1d814441ffe6QmxiENmg3wjTp","messageID":"msg_1e2920b74001Ivn2LxOAgILdTJ","type":"tool","id":"call_3fd6b2a93a6a4df2ad526f36","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Iteration 6: Offer coverage on the fresh plain rows, and the inverted depth gate\n\n## Focus\n\nClose the source-diversity gap that blocks convergence, and with it verify the one claim R1 rests on that this lane had not measured itself: what the brief actually offered across the twenty fresh plain rows, per runtime.\n\n## Actions Taken\n\n1. Counted the offered command on each of the twenty `fresh-fit-*` rows, per runtime, in the on arm run 1.\n2. Compared each offer with the row's `expected_command` and read the three rows whose offer is a different command.\n3. Searched the whole fresh set for the depth vocabulary to find every row R1 could touch.\n4. Read the hook's replay path to confirm the run-line offer is the hook's own output, not a runner guess.\n5. Registered the sources for the questions with their evidence class so the coverage graph can score diversity.\n\n## Findings\n\n1. The on-arm brief carries a command on 7 of the 20 fresh plain rows, and the count is identical on all five runtimes: 7 of 20. The other 13 rows carry no command at all. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/scratch/runs/claude.jsonl:1]\n2. Five of the seven offers are the row's expected command (`/create:readme`, `/create:goal`, `/design:chart`, `/design:diagram`, and `/doctor:agents-md check` for the `/doctor:agents-md` family). Two are a different doctor command: `/doctor:setup` where the row wants `/doctor:env`, and `/doctor:overlay status` where it wants `/doctor:update`. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/behaviour-fresh-prompts.jsonl:11]\n3. None of the five ask-policy plain rows carries a command: the changelog row, the deep-research row, the deep-review row, the design-extract row and the skill-advisor doctor row all reach the model as a skill with no runnable command. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/scratch/runs/claude.jsonl:1]\n4. The depth gate is inverted on the only two fresh rows that use a depth phrase. `fresh-fit-18` asks for \"a thorough multi-pass review\" and expects `/deep:review`; `fresh-decline-refusal-02` says \"skip the deep review\" and expects nothing. The brief offers `/deep:review` on the refusal and not on the request, on all five runtimes. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/behaviour-fresh-prompts.jsonl:18]\n5. R1 must therefore be two-sided. A prose depth-phrase rule that only reads refusals would remove the false offer on the refusal row and leave the missing offer on the real request; the same change must prove both rows. Confirmation: one render replay shows `/deep:review` in `fresh-fit-18`'s head and not in the refusal row's head. [INFERENCE: from findings 4 and the attach gate at command-attach.ts:510]\n6. The 13 no-command rows are not all failures: a skill-only route is counted as followed by the arm's own metric, so 7 of 20 is an offer-surface count, not a success rate. What it does bound is the reach of the policy word: a model cannot act on a `(start)` or `(ask)` word the brief never printed. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:2199]\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- Treating 13 of 20 as 13 failures: the arm's metric follows a skill path, so the count is about the offer surface only.\n- Blaming the runner for the missing offers: `replayOffer` spawns the hook with the row's prompt and reads the head it returns, so the run line records the hook's own output.\n\n## Dead Ends\n\n- A stored head for `fresh-fit-18`: the run line records the offer fields, not the rendered string, so the cause of the missing command needs one hook replay of that prompt.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- Ambiguous input: \"no command\" can mean the route chose a skill-only path or the attach gate withheld a command. The run line cannot separate them; both leave the model without a runnable command, which is what this lane measures.\n- Contradictory evidence: iteration 4's R1 was scoped from the refusal row only. This iteration shows the same vocabulary has one request row, so the recommendation is amended rather than withdrawn.\n- Missing dependencies: no hook replay was run, because this lane must not run the repo's tooling; the cause of the `fresh-fit-18` miss is named as the next check.\n- Partial success: the offer counts are per runtime and agree exactly, so the measurement is solid; the cause of each miss is not.\n\n## Questions Answered\n\n- None new. All four lane questions were already answered; this iteration strengthens their evidence.\n\n## Questions Remaining\n\n- None. The confirmation runs named in the recommendations are follow-up work, not open questions.\n\n## Sources Consulted\n\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/scratch/runs/claude.jsonl:1`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/behaviour-fresh-prompts.jsonl:11`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs:100`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:2199`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:510`\n\n## Assessment\n\n- New information ratio: 0.85\n- Questions addressed: the offer-surface coverage and R1's scope\n- Questions answered: none new (all four were already answered)\n\n## Reflection\n\n- What worked and why: counting per row instead of trusting the aggregate exposed the strongest number in this lane — 7 of 20 offers, identical everywhere — and the depth gate's inversion fell out of the same pass.\n- What did not work and why: the first attempt to compute plain-row offers with a shell join returned zero and was wrong; the field is present on the raw line, so the join had failed, not the data. Re-reading one line before trusting the aggregate caught it.\n- What I would do differently: start every arm question with a per-row dump of the field being counted; the aggregate names are not the row names.\n\n## Recommended Next Focus\n\nNone for research. Synthesis should carry the 7-of-20 offer coverage, the ask-policy zero, and the two-sided R1 as the lane's headline results.\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux-5/iterations/iteration-006.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux-5/iterations/iteration-006.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux-5/iterations/iteration-006.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Iteration 6: Offer coverage on the fresh plain rows, and the inverted depth gate\\n\\n## Focus\\n\\nClose the source-diversity gap that blocks convergence, and with it verify the one claim R1 rests on that this lane had not measured itself: what the brief actually offered across the twenty fresh plain rows, per runtime.\\n\\n## Actions Taken\\n\\n1. Counted the offered command on each of the twenty `fresh-fit-*` rows, per runtime, in the on arm run 1.\\n2. Compared each offer with the row's `expected_command` and read the three rows whose offer is a different command.\\n3. Searched the whole fresh set for the depth vocabulary to find every row R1 could touch.\\n4. Read the hook's replay path to confirm the run-line offer is the hook's own output, not a runner guess.\\n5. Registered the sources for the questions with their evidence class so the coverage graph can score diversity.\\n\\n## Findings\\n\\n1. The on-arm brief carries a command on 7 of the 20 fresh plain rows, and the count is identical on all five runtimes: 7 of 20. The other 13 rows carry no command at all. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/scratch/runs/claude.jsonl:1]\\n2. Five of the seven offers are the row's expected command (`/create:readme`, `/create:goal`, `/design:chart`, `/design:diagram`, and `/doctor:agents-md check` for the `/doctor:agents-md` family). Two are a different doctor command: `/doctor:setup` where the row wants `/doctor:env`, and `/doctor:overlay status` where it wants `/doctor:update`. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/behaviour-fresh-prompts.jsonl:11]\\n3. None of the five ask-policy plain rows carries a command: the changelog row, the deep-research row, the deep-review row, the design-extract row and the skill-advisor doctor row all reach the model as a skill with no runnable command. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/scratch/runs/claude.jsonl:1]\\n4. The depth gate is inverted on the only two fresh rows that use a depth phrase. `fresh-fit-18` asks for \\\"a thorough multi-pass review\\\" and expects `/deep:review`; `fresh-decline-refusal-02` says \\\"skip the deep review\\\" and expects nothing. The brief offers `/deep:review` on the refusal and not on the request, on all five runtimes. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/behaviour-fresh-prompts.jsonl:18]\\n5. R1 must therefore be two-sided. A prose depth-phrase rule that only reads refusals would remove the false offer on the refusal row and leave the missing offer on the real request; the same change must prove both rows. Confirmation: one render replay shows `/deep:review` in `fresh-fit-18`'s head and not in the refusal row's head. [INFERENCE: from findings 4 and the attach gate at command-attach.ts:510]\\n6. The 13 no-command rows are not all failures: a skill-only route is counted as followed by the arm's own metric, so 7 of 20 is an offer-surface count, not a success rate. What it does bound is the reach of the policy word: a model cannot act on a `(start)` or `(ask)` word the brief never printed. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:2199]\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- Treating 13 of 20 as 13 failures: the arm's metric follows a skill path, so the count is about the offer surface only.\\n- Blaming the runner for the missing offers: `replayOffer` spawns the hook with the row's prompt and reads the head it returns, so the run line records the hook's own output.\\n\\n## Dead Ends\\n\\n- A stored head for `fresh-fit-18`: the run line records the offer fields, not the rendered string, so the cause of the missing command needs one hook replay of that prompt.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- Ambiguous input: \\\"no command\\\" can mean the route chose a skill-only path or the attach gate withheld a command. The run line cannot separate them; both leave the model without a runnable command, which is what this lane measures.\\n- Contradictory evidence: iteration 4's R1 was scoped from the refusal row only. This iteration shows the same vocabulary has one request row, so the recommendation is amended rather than withdrawn.\\n- Missing dependencies: no hook replay was run, because this lane must not run the repo's tooling; the cause of the `fresh-fit-18` miss is named as the next check.\\n- Partial success: the offer counts are per runtime and agree exactly, so the measurement is solid; the cause of each miss is not.\\n\\n## Questions Answered\\n\\n- None new. All four lane questions were already answered; this iteration strengthens their evidence.\\n\\n## Questions Remaining\\n\\n- None. The confirmation runs named in the recommendations are follow-up work, not open questions.\\n\\n## Sources Consulted\\n\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/scratch/runs/claude.jsonl:1`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/behaviour-fresh-prompts.jsonl:11`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs:100`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:2199`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:510`\\n\\n## Assessment\\n\\n- New information ratio: 0.85\\n- Questions addressed: the offer-surface coverage and R1's scope\\n- Questions answered: none new (all four were already answered)\\n\\n## Reflection\\n\\n- What worked and why: counting per row instead of trusting the aggregate exposed the strongest number in this lane — 7 of 20 offers, identical everywhere — and the depth gate's inversion fell out of the same pass.\\n- What did not work and why: the first attempt to compute plain-row offers with a shell join returned zero and was wrong; the field is present on the raw line, so the join had failed, not the data. Re-reading one line before trusting the aggregate caught it.\\n- What I would do differently: start every arm question with a per-row dump of the field being counted; the aggregate names are not the row names.\\n\\n## Recommended Next Focus\\n\\nNone for research. Synthesis should carry the 7-of-20 offer coverage, the ask-policy zero, and the two-sided R1 as the lane's headline results.\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux-5/iterations/iteration-006.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794802589266,"end":1794802603168}}}}
