{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794802724814,"sessionID":"ses_e1d814441ffe6QmxiENmg3wjTp","part":{"partID":"prt_1e29407c1001Wtsb38x11cjlrZ","sessionID":"ses_e1d814441ffe6QmxiENmg3wjTp","messageID":"msg_1e293ebed001jWjhD4A7I1DgdC","type":"tool","id":"call_703b2d2a31a5420b8f3fe014","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Iteration 7: Claims audit, each load-bearing claim against two sources\n\n## Focus\n\nRegister the lane's load-bearing claims as verified claims, each with the two independent sources that support it and the check that would falsify it, so the coverage graph's claim-verification signal rests on evidence rather than on the absence of a claim.\n\n## Actions Taken\n\n1. Listed every claim the lane's recommendations rest on.\n2. Paired each claim with a code or corpus source and a measured or phase source.\n3. Re-checked the two claims that had only one source class.\n4. Registered the claims with their verification status and source edges.\n\n## Findings\n\n1. Claim C1, the mention guard only fires on a typed command: verified by the guard's own regex entry point and by the refusal row, which carries the prose phrase and still drew the offer on all five runtimes. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:414]\n2. Claim C2, five of eight fresh decline rows carry a command: verified by the fresh row definitions and by the per-row offer fields in the run lines, which agree exactly across five runtimes and both arms. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/scratch/runs/dsh.jsonl:1]\n3. Claim C3, the brief carries a command on 7 of 20 fresh plain rows and on none of the five ask rows: verified by the run lines on all five runtimes and by the corpus row labels that name the expected command and policy. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/behaviour-fresh-prompts.jsonl:16]\n4. Claim C4, Claude starts none of its ten start-policy rows: verified by the per-policy summary block and by two raw run lines (`fresh-fit-01`, `fresh-fit-03`) that show the offer, exit 0 and zero changed paths. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/scratch/runs/claude.jsonl:1]\n5. Claim C5, the policy vocabulary is defined outside the brief: verified by the root doc's four-sentence definition and by the render, which prints the word without a definition. [SOURCE: AGENTS.md:68]\n6. The one claim this lane could not verify to two source classes is the attention-dilution inference: the byte split is measured, but no arm moved the directive tail, so it stays an inference with a stated confirmation path and is not registered as a claim. [INFERENCE: from the 218-byte fixed tail and the absent A/B]\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- Registering the attention-dilution inference as a verified claim: its evidence is one byte measurement and no behavioural contrast.\n- Using a single source class for C3: the run lines and the corpus labels are independent records of the same row.\n\n## Dead Ends\n\n- A second measured source for the directive's effect on attention: none exists in the packet.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- Ambiguous input: \"verified\" could mean reproduced by a rerun or confirmed by two independent records. This lane uses the second meaning and says so.\n- Contradictory evidence: none. The raw rows and the summary blocks agree.\n- Missing dependencies: no rerun of the arm is possible in this lane.\n- Partial success: C1 through C5 are registered; the inference is excluded by design.\n\n## Questions Answered\n\n- None new. All four lane questions were answered earlier.\n\n## Questions Remaining\n\n- None.\n\n## Sources Consulted\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:414`\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/scratch/runs/dsh.jsonl:1`\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/scratch/runs/claude.jsonl:1`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/behaviour-fresh-prompts.jsonl:16`\n- `AGENTS.md:68`\n\n## Assessment\n\n- New information ratio: 0.20\n- Questions addressed: the evidence status of each claim\n- Questions answered: none new\n\n## Reflection\n\n- What worked and why: pairing a code or corpus source with a measured source per claim caught that the attention inference had only one class, which is why it is excluded rather than promoted.\n- What did not work and why: the graph's claim signal treats a claim with no status as unverified, so an unregistered claim silently held convergence at zero; the fix is to register claims with their status, not to avoid claiming.\n- What I would do differently: register claims as they are found instead of at the end.\n\n## Recommended Next Focus\n\nNone. The lane is ready for synthesis.\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux-5/iterations/iteration-007.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux-5/iterations/iteration-007.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux-5/iterations/iteration-007.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Iteration 7: Claims audit, each load-bearing claim against two sources\\n\\n## Focus\\n\\nRegister the lane's load-bearing claims as verified claims, each with the two independent sources that support it and the check that would falsify it, so the coverage graph's claim-verification signal rests on evidence rather than on the absence of a claim.\\n\\n## Actions Taken\\n\\n1. Listed every claim the lane's recommendations rest on.\\n2. Paired each claim with a code or corpus source and a measured or phase source.\\n3. Re-checked the two claims that had only one source class.\\n4. Registered the claims with their verification status and source edges.\\n\\n## Findings\\n\\n1. Claim C1, the mention guard only fires on a typed command: verified by the guard's own regex entry point and by the refusal row, which carries the prose phrase and still drew the offer on all five runtimes. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:414]\\n2. Claim C2, five of eight fresh decline rows carry a command: verified by the fresh row definitions and by the per-row offer fields in the run lines, which agree exactly across five runtimes and both arms. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/scratch/runs/dsh.jsonl:1]\\n3. Claim C3, the brief carries a command on 7 of 20 fresh plain rows and on none of the five ask rows: verified by the run lines on all five runtimes and by the corpus row labels that name the expected command and policy. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/behaviour-fresh-prompts.jsonl:16]\\n4. Claim C4, Claude starts none of its ten start-policy rows: verified by the per-policy summary block and by two raw run lines (`fresh-fit-01`, `fresh-fit-03`) that show the offer, exit 0 and zero changed paths. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/scratch/runs/claude.jsonl:1]\\n5. Claim C5, the policy vocabulary is defined outside the brief: verified by the root doc's four-sentence definition and by the render, which prints the word without a definition. [SOURCE: AGENTS.md:68]\\n6. The one claim this lane could not verify to two source classes is the attention-dilution inference: the byte split is measured, but no arm moved the directive tail, so it stays an inference with a stated confirmation path and is not registered as a claim. [INFERENCE: from the 218-byte fixed tail and the absent A/B]\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- Registering the attention-dilution inference as a verified claim: its evidence is one byte measurement and no behavioural contrast.\\n- Using a single source class for C3: the run lines and the corpus labels are independent records of the same row.\\n\\n## Dead Ends\\n\\n- A second measured source for the directive's effect on attention: none exists in the packet.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- Ambiguous input: \\\"verified\\\" could mean reproduced by a rerun or confirmed by two independent records. This lane uses the second meaning and says so.\\n- Contradictory evidence: none. The raw rows and the summary blocks agree.\\n- Missing dependencies: no rerun of the arm is possible in this lane.\\n- Partial success: C1 through C5 are registered; the inference is excluded by design.\\n\\n## Questions Answered\\n\\n- None new. All four lane questions were answered earlier.\\n\\n## Questions Remaining\\n\\n- None.\\n\\n## Sources Consulted\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:414`\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/scratch/runs/dsh.jsonl:1`\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/scratch/runs/claude.jsonl:1`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/behaviour-fresh-prompts.jsonl:16`\\n- `AGENTS.md:68`\\n\\n## Assessment\\n\\n- New information ratio: 0.20\\n- Questions addressed: the evidence status of each claim\\n- Questions answered: none new\\n\\n## Reflection\\n\\n- What worked and why: pairing a code or corpus source with a measured source per claim caught that the attention inference had only one class, which is why it is excluded rather than promoted.\\n- What did not work and why: the graph's claim signal treats a claim with no status as unverified, so an unregistered claim silently held convergence at zero; the fix is to register claims with their status, not to avoid claiming.\\n- What I would do differently: register claims as they are found instead of at the end.\\n\\n## Recommended Next Focus\\n\\nNone. The lane is ready for synthesis.\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux-5/iterations/iteration-007.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794802714561,"end":1794802724814}}}}
