of 24) and the fresh sample (5 of 8) are different samples and are not pooled.\n107: - The registry keys are read from the lane's own deltas; the lead's merge owns the cross-lane registry.\n108: - Only five runtimes were measured. Codex is not in the arm (Q075).\n109: \n110: ## 11. Open Questions\n111: \n112: None in this lane. The confirmation runs in section 9 are follow-up work, not open questions.\n113: \n114: ## 12. Eliminated Alternatives\n115: \n116: - **A brief policy legend.** Withdrawn: `AGENTS.md` already defines `run`, `start` and `ask`, and a second definition spends bytes on every brief.\n117: - **Gating `/create:changelog` by command name.** Eliminated: the release-date row carries no small-edit phrase, so the gate would not fire.\n118: - **Treating an offer on a decline row as a safety failure.** Eliminated: 49 of 50 decline-row offers produced no start; the failure needs the model action too.\n119: - **Truncation as a wording defect.** Eliminated: the 80-token cap is far above the 88-byte measured head.\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 120]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux-5/research.md, lines 98-119\n98: | R2 | Add a single-value edit phrase (release date, version number) to the small-edit vocabulary, not the changelog command | 1 of 8 decline rows | `fresh-decline-small-edit-02` prints no command; `fresh-fit-16` keeps `/create:changelog`; the typo-fix changelog test keeps its command | Low: one phrase; phase 020's three-failure gate history is the caution |\n99: | R3 | Withdrawn. Do not add a policy legend to the brief | `AGENTS.md` defines the vocabulary for every measured runtime | n/a | n/a |\n100: | R4 | Measure Claude's start-policy silence on the ten rows after phase 016's 44-of-44 listing | 0 of 10 starts, 0 capped, identical brief | A Claude-only run shows any start above zero, or names the runtime limit | None to other runtimes |\n101: | R5 | Split the decline target between offer fit and model path choice | 1 substituted start; dsh acted with no tracked workflow on 5 of 28 on-arm rows | The next arm reports offers and starts separately on decline rows | None: a reporting change |\n102: \n103: ## 10. Limits\n104: \n105: - No model run, no rerun of the arm, no hook replay. The cause of the missing offer on `fresh-fit-18` is not established; the next check is one hook replay of that prompt, read for the recommendation list and the head.\n106: - The sealed fit sample (8 of 24) and the fresh sample (5 of 8) are different samples and are not pooled.\n107: - The registry keys are read from the lane's own deltas; the lead's merge owns the cross-lane registry.\n108: - Only five runtimes were measured. Codex is not in the arm (Q075).\n109: \n110: ## 11. Open Questions\n111: \n112: None in this lane. The confirmation runs in section 9 are follow-up work, not open questions.\n113: \n114: ## 12. Eliminated Alternatives\n115: \n116: - **A brief policy legend.** Withdrawn: `AGENTS.md` already defines `run`, `start` and `ask`, and a second definition spends bytes on every brief.\n117: - **Gating `/create:changelog` by command name.** Eliminated: the release-date row carries no small-edit phrase, so the gate would not fire.\n118: - **Treating an offer on a decline row as a safety failure.** Eliminated: 49 of 50 decline-row offers produced no start; the failure needs the model action too.\n119: - **Truncation as a wording defect.** Eliminated: the 80-token cap is far above the 88-byte measured head.\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 120]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"limit\":22,\"offset\":98,\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/linea